itory Library Program (FDLP).  aDirector and producer, Randy G. Masten ; assistant director, Peter Wood ; writer, Peter Wood ; contributing writer, Randy G. Masten ; executive producers, COL Andrew Steadman, Don Wright ; video, Kyle Davis.  a"This Army documentary provides an overview of the United States Pacific Command (USPACOM). It examines China's current worldview, and its rapid rise in force projection capabilities. The film looks at the People's Liberation Army (PLA), Chinese military history, and breaks down the size and scope of the PLA's forces. China's military doctrine is discussed including small and large-island seizure operations, as well as the phases of amphibious landing operations"--DVIDS website.1 aClosed captioning available in English  aDescription based on online resource; title from landing page (dvidshub.net, viewed July 31, 2026).10aUnited States.bPacific Command.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n5007618510aChina.bZhongguo ren min jie fang jun.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n79092531 0aAmphibious warfare.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85004611 0aDeployment (Strategy)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85037035 0aPacific AreaxStrategic aspects. 0aMilitary art and sciencezChina. 7aDocumentary films.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026205 7aNonfiction films.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026423 7aInternet videos.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110263371 aMasten, Randy,efilm director.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20210119031 aWood, Peterc(Analyst),efilm director.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20220380321 aSteadman, Andrew,efilm producer.1 aWright, Donald P.,d1964-efilm producer.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20080261952 aArmy University Press (U.S.),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no201712362040uhttps://purl.fdlp.gov/GPO/gpo258699704 zAddress at ti